  "development_type": "Certificates of Lawful Development",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The evidence submitted demonstrates that, on the balance of probability, the rear ground floor has been used as a single self-contained dwellinghouse (Use Class C3) for a continuous period of at least four years prior to the date of this application. As such, the use has become immune from enforcement action under Section 171B(2) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and is therefore lawful under Section 191 of the same Act."
